  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Dissolve ingredients (except vitamins and cysteine), adjust pH to 5.5 with 10 N H2SO4 and sparge medium with 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture for 30 – 45 min to make it anoxic."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials (e.g., 20 ml of medium in 50 ml bottles) and autoclave."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Prior to inoculation add vitamins (sterilized by filtration) and cysteine from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Adjust pH of complete medium to 5.5 - 6.0, if necessary."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "After inoculation pressurize vials to 0.5 bar overpressure with sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "First dissolve NTA in 200 ml of distilled water and adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH, then dissolve mineral salts."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "Finally adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH and make up to 1000.00 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}